      "card_ids": ["C21", "C25"]
    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct experimental oral bioavailability data exist for the query molecule itself.",
    "No measured permeability or nucleoside transporter data exist for the 5-hydroxyimidazole-4-carboxamide riboside scaffold.",
    "The query is more polar and more ionized at pH 7.4 than all reference nucleosides, so whether its F falls below 20% remains uncertain.",
    "No data address first-pass metabolism, clearance, or formulation effects for the query.",
    "Didanosine L2 variability introduces class-level uncertainty, but no card provides an affirmative threshold-relevant F < 20% outcome."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "New L2 records do not overturn the level 1 decision. They clarify food and dose effects for rufinamide, confirm emtricitabine's 92% F in a fixed-dose combination, and show didanosine variability without establishing F < 20%. All measured nucleoside contexts remain at or above 20%, and no card provides affirmative threshold-relevant evidence below 20%. Prediction remains high with moderate confidence."
}

